{"tool": "patent_search", "success": true, "data": {"query": "immersive CAVE display movable wall screen projection mapping viewpoint adaptation", "requested_sources": ["arxiv"], "sources": ["arxiv"], "actual_sources_used": ["arxiv"], "source_result_counts": {"arxiv": 5}, "source_status": {"arxiv": {"success": true, "count": 5, "error": null}}, "unavailable_or_empty_sources": [], "skipped_sources": [], "empty_sources": [], "unavailable_reasons": {}, "search_results": [{"reference_id": "1712.08469v1", "title": "Wall modeling via function enrichment: extension to detached-eddy simulation", "publication_date": null, "applicant": null, "abstract": "We extend the approach of wall modeling via function enrichment to detached-eddy simulation. The wall model aims at using coarse cells in the near-wall region by modeling the velocity profile in the viscous sublayer and log-layer. However, unlike other wall models, the full Navier-Stokes equations are still discretely fulfilled, including the pressure gradient and convective term. This is achieved by enriching the elements of the high-order discontinuous Galerkin method with the law-of-the-wall.", "similarity_score": 0.5, "key_claims": [], "technical_differences": [], "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/1712.08469v1", "source": "arxiv", "patent_id": "1712.08469v1", "relevance_score": 0.5}, {"reference_id": "1610.08205v1", "title": "Wall modeling via function enrichment within a high-order DG method for RANS simulations of incompressible flow", "publication_date": null, "applicant": null, "abstract": "We present a novel approach to wall modeling for RANS within the discontinuous Galerkin method. Wall functions are not used to prescribe boundary conditions as usual but they are built into the function space of the numerical method as a local enrichment, in addition to the standard polynomial component. The Galerkin method then automatically finds the optimal solution among all shape functions available. This idea is fully consistent and gives the wall model vast flexibility in separated bounda", "similarity_score": 0.5, "key_claims": [], "technical_differences": [], "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/1610.08205v1", "source": "arxiv", "patent_id": "1610.08205v1", "relevance_score": 0.5}, {"reference_id": "1705.08813v2", "title": "A multiscale approach to hybrid RANS/LES wall modeling within a high-order discontinuous Galerkin scheme using function enrichment", "publication_date": null, "applicant": null, "abstract": "We present a novel approach to hybrid RANS/LES wall modeling based on function enrichment, which overcomes the common problem of the RANS-LES transition and enables coarse meshes near the boundary. While the concept of function enrichment as an efficient discretization technique for turbulent boundary layers has been proposed in an earlier article by Krank & Wall (J. Comput. Phys. 316 (2016) 94-116), the contribution of this work is a rigorous derivation of a new multiscale turbulence modeling a", "similarity_score": 0.5, "key_claims": [], "technical_differences": [], "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/1705.08813v2", "source": "arxiv", "patent_id": "1705.08813v2", "relevance_score": 0.5}, {"reference_id": "2511.12251v1", "title": "Locomotion in CAVE: Enhancing Immersion through Full-Body Motion", "publication_date": null, "applicant": null, "abstract": "Cave Automatic Virtual Environment (CAVE) is one of the virtual reality (VR) immersive devices currently used to present virtual environments. However, the locomotion methods in the CAVE are limited by unnatural interaction methods, severely hindering the user experience and immersion in the CAVE. We proposed a locomotion framework for CAVE environments aimed at enhancing the immersive locomotion experience through optimized human motion recognition technology. Firstly, we construct a four-sided", "similarity_score": 0.5, "key_claims": [], "technical_differences": [], "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2511.12251v1", "source": "arxiv", "patent_id": "2511.12251v1", "relevance_score": 0.5}, {"reference_id": "2508.10952v1", "title": "On 2-Movable Total Domination in the Join and Corona of Graphs", "publication_date": null, "applicant": null, "abstract": "Let $G$ be a connected graph. A non-empty $T\\subseteq V(G)$ is a $2$-\\textit{movable total dominating set} of $G$ if $T$ is a total dominating set and for every pair $x,y \\in T$, $T \\backslash \\{x, y\\}$ is a total dominating set in $G$, or there exist $u, v \\in V(G) \\backslash T$ such that $u$ and $v$ are adjacent to $x$ and $y$, respectively, and $(T \\backslash \\{x,y\\}) \\cup \\{u,v\\}$ is a total dominating set in $G$. The $2$-\\textit{movable total domination number} of $G$, denoted by $γ_{mt}^{2", "similarity_score": 0.5, "key_claims": [], "technical_differences": [], "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2508.10952v1", "source": "arxiv", "patent_id": "2508.10952v1", "relevance_score": 0.5}], "total_found": 5, "search_strategy": "real_data_source_query", "source_handling_policy": "Unavailable or disabled sources were skipped and recorded. Do not block the phase when other verifiable evidence exists; if no verifiable evidence exists, revise keywords and try other real sources.", "keywords_used": ["immersive CAVE display movable wall screen projection mapping viewpoint adaptation"]}, "timestamp": "2026-06-18T03:24:44.468965", "duration_ms": 2000.8010000000002}

